# Not written:
#   ADMIN-SSH (port2): the rule is for zone port2, and a security rule names no zone: give the networks behind it with --zone-network
#   ADMIN-SSH (port1): the rule is for zone port1, and a security rule names no zone: give the networks behind it with --zone-network
#   WEB-IN: not converted: action Dst NAT: how the API spells its target list is not known, so the translation is not read
#   DNS-OUT: disabled in the source
#   UPDATES: host name object updates.example.com (IPv4): a security rule names addresses
#   TO-LAB: not converted: action Cascade: the rules of the rule list it hands traffic to are not read, and they decide that traffic
#   ODD: schedule '{"type": "recurring", "name": "Work-Hours"}' is not converted; the rule would apply at all times
